1
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,999
[Music] My name is Amala George. I'm from Anand, Gujarat.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:22,999
The first person in our family to take the covenant was my mother. She took the covenant in 2019. From that moment onward, I too began living the covenant life.

3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,999
At that time, I didn’t really have any particular needs, but my mother told me, “You should also live a covenant life.” So I did.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:36,999
While living that way, I came here and prayed, asking Mother Mary which college I should go to for my M.Sc.

5
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,999
And Mother gave me the name of a college. I went to that very college for my M.Sc.

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,999
But it wasn’t as easy as I thought it would be.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,999
I faced terrible mental harassment there. One day, the Dean, a lady, called me into a meeting and said,

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:57,999
“I will make sure you fail. Don’t expect any help from me no matter what happens.” I was terrified.

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,999
She even started taking steps to detain me. I had no idea why—

10
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:09,999
There was no personal enmity between us. We’d never even met before. I still don’t know why she had such hatred toward me.

11
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,999
I was terribly afraid. I was good at studies, but that fear completely overtook me and clouded my mind.

12
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,999
Even when I went to write the exam, I had only one fear: What if she fails me now? What will happen to my life then?

13
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:31,999
Because of that fear, I forgot everything I had studied. I went to that exam holding the covenant medal.

14
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:41,999
I touched the covenant Medal and prayed to Mother Mary, saying, “Mother, I give up. I’m done studying. I can’t take this torture anymore.”

15
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,999
I closed my pen and got up to hand in my answer sheet. But just then, our supervisor came near me and said, “write whatever you know.”

16
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,999
Suddenly, I felt like Mother was speaking directly to me. And so, I started writing.

17
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,999
As I continued, it was as if someone was guiding me mentally—telling me, “This is the answer to this question, and this one to that.”

18
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,999
I kept writing. When the results came,

19
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,999
I had not just passed—I topped the university that semester. And in every semester after that, I was the university topper.

20
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:18,999
Then came the final semester of my M.Sc., and we had a six-month dissertation period.

21
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:24,999
My dissertation guide was a staunch atheist. She didn’t believe in God at all.

22
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:29,999
She didn’t like that I regularly went to church and prayed.

23
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,999
Because of that, she started torturing me severely—especially mentally.

24
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:40,999
She overloaded me with work. She’d say, “You have to come at 7 AM, do this, do that.”

25
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:46,999
I told her, “Ma’am, I can’t come that early because I attend Mass every morning.”

26
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:53,999
I said, “I’ll come after Mass. I can even work overtime in the evening, but I can’t miss Mass.”

27
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:58,999
She agreed to the overtime part but never eased up on me.

28
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:06,999
At the same time, there was another student under her—a PhD student—who was also being tortured by her.

29
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,999
Because of that torture, he abandoned his project halfway and left.

30
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,999
The teacher then dumped his entire project responsibility onto me as well.

31
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,999
I was under extreme stress. I couldn’t even finish my own project, let alone his.

32
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:25,999
No matter how much I did, she would keep rejecting it, saying, “This is wrong, this isn’t acceptable.”

33
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:30,999
I was deeply distressed. When I’d walk into college, my classmates would look at me and mock me.

34
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:35,999
“She’s the one who always goes to church. She’s always praying. And still, look—God isn’t helping her. She’s still suffering.”

35
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:42,999
It hurt me so much. But I’d look straight at them and say, “My God has a plan for me. Whatever it is, it’s for my good.”

36
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:48,999
“Even if I cry today, it’s okay. My God will do what needs to be done.” I believed that with all my heart.

37
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:54,999
When I looked at my mother, and when I looked at Mother Mary of Kreupasanam, I had no words—I could only cry.

38
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:59,999
For months, I just sat there and cried. “Mother, I don’t know what to do.

39
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:04,999
I only have three months left. I have to complete both my project and that other student’s project too.

40
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:09,999
Only then will I get my degree on time.”

41
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,999
I kept crying and praying. I always kept the covenant locket of Kreupasanam Mother Mary close to me while studying.

42
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,999
Whenever I had a doubt, I wouldn’t ask a person—I’d ask Mother Mary directly.

43
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:23,999
“Mother, I don’t understand this. What should I do?” And it would truly feel like she herself was answering me—

44
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,999
just like a real mother speaking to her daughter.

45
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:32,999
She would guide me step by step: “Dear, do this. Now do that.”

46
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:38,999
One day, I was sitting with my laptop, wondering, “What should I do now?”

47
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,999
Suddenly, a paper appeared on my web page—even though I hadn’t searched for anything.

48
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:45,999
I opened and started reading it, and I felt Mother say in my heart,

49
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:54,999
“Whatever method is shown in this paper, close your eyes and follow it.”I followed it. And within just three weeks, I completed the entire project.

50
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:00,999
I completed writing my full dissertation thesis and submitted it. As a result, I passed with excellent marks.

51
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:05,999
Not only that—I even received a Gold Medal from the university.

52
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:13,999
I was the university topper. Because in the Microbiology Department, no one had ever received such high marks before.

53
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,999
That’s how Mother helped me pass my Master’s degree with such distinction.

54
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:21,999
After that, I had a deep desire to pursue a PhD.

55
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:26,999
But I wasn’t sure what subject to choose or which one had better scope.

56
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:32,999
So again, I began praying to Mother: “Mother, what should I do next? Which subject should I take? I’m confused.”

57
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:39,999
Around that time, my friends told me, “The government isn’t really providing funds these days.

58
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:45,999
If you’re hoping for funding, don’t get your hopes up. The central government has stopped most of the schemes.”

59
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:51,999
I felt terribly discouraged. That’s when my father told me about something called Daily Bread—a time of daily prayer.

60
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:58,999
I started joining in that prayer time. I would cry during Daily Bread and pray: “Mother, I don’t have any other option. If I don’t get this PhD,

61
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:05,999
then I’ll have to waste one whole year preparing for competitive exams. I don’t have that kind of time.”

62
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:12,999
I prayed earnestly. And as an answer to that prayer, within six months, that government fund reopened.

63
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,999
I was told I could now apply.

64
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:22,999
I went to my university to collect all my documents. But my Dean was still a little bitter.

65
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:28,999
When I spoke to my HOD (Head of Department), he said, “All your documents are already in the university office.

66
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:33,999
The Dean doesn’t have a single one. You go directly to the university.”

67
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:39,999
He said, “They all tried hard to make sure you didn’t get the gold medal, that you would fail.

68
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:43,999
But suddenly one day, we got a call from the university telling us:

69
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:47,999
‘We need all the documents of this girl. You can’t keep them at your department anymore.’”

70
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:51,999
So I immediately went to the university, and they treated me well.

71
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:55,999
They said, “You don’t have to worry. Within two days, we’ll give you all the certificates you need.”

72
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:01,999
Then my teacher asked me, “Which subject are you going to take for your PhD?”

73
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,999
While I was praying, the subject I received was Neuroscience.

74
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,999
But Neuroscience had nothing to do with my Master’s.

75
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,999
I studied Microbiology.

76
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,999
But I felt in my heart that Mother told me to take Neuroscience.

77
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:18,999
I told my teacher, “This is what I feel from Mother Mary. I believe I should take Neuroscience for my PhD.”

78
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,999
She looked surprised and asked, “But what you studied and this subject have no connection.

79
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:25,999
How will you even get into Neuroscience with your background?”

80
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:31,999
That hurt me. I prayed again: “Mother, I don’t know how this will work, but since You said it, I will go ahead with it.”

81
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:37,999
Then I started writing my project proposal, but nothing I wrote seemed right.

82
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:43,999
Still, I always had Mother’s covenant locket with me while reading and studying.

83
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:51,999
I told Mother, “Christmas is on the 25th. I want to submit my final application on Christmas Day.

84
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:56,999
Please, Mother, help me complete a solid project proposal by then.”

85
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:04,999
While I was trying to write, suddenly it felt like someone was dictating everything to me.

86
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:09,999
I just wrote down word for word everything I felt was being spoken to me.

87
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:13,999
That’s how I completed my proposal. On December 25th, I submitted it to the government.

88
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:19,999
I printed a copy of that proposal, and on the front I wrote:

89
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,999
“Not by merit, but by grace.”

90
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:31,999
Because if you looked at my education or background, the central government had no obligation to give me funding for that subject.

91
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:38,999
Only one person could help me now—Mother Mary. At Kreupasanam during Daily Bread, Father would always say:

92
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:43,999
“If you have your documents, hold them in your hands and pray during Daily Bread.”

93
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:49,999
So I followed his instruction. I gathered all my documents and prayed with them.

94
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:57,999
I told Mother, “I’m in Gujarat. I can’t come there and show this to You in person.

95
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:01,999
But You can go anywhere, Mother. Please go on my behalf. I have no other way.”

96
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:08,999
“I did everything the way You told me. Everyone around me said it wouldn’t happen, but You’re my only hope.”

97
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:16,999
And then on February 14, 2025, I received an email from the Central Government:

98
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:22,999
Your funding has been sanctioned. You can now apply to any university across India.

99
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:29,999
I began praying again — “Mother, which university should I go to? Which guide should I choose? How should I continue my studies?”

100
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:35,999
I had only one condition: wherever I go, the person guiding me should never stop me from going to church. I must always be able to attend Holy Mass.

101
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:45,999
I prayed for a university, college, and hostel close to a church. I just can’t live away from the church. I’ve grown up that way. Whether it’s raining or sunny…

102
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:56,999
My parents would always take me to church — even with a raincoat on. I have never missed Mass. It’s not possible for me to live without it. That’s how much it matters to me.

103
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:05,999
So I prayed. And as a result of that prayer, I casually applied to a university. But halfway through the process, I let it go.

104
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:10,999
Then my mom told me again — “Apply to the same university, but this time for the Neuroscience department.”

105
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:16,999
So I started reading the profiles of professors in that university’s neuroscience department.

106
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:21,999
As I was going through them, one particular professor’s profile came up, and I felt something in my heart.

107
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:28,999
A voice told me — “This is the one. Read this professor’s profile. You should send an email to this professor.” So I followed that.

108
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:37,999
I read his profile carefully. I prepared a project proposal, my CV, my results, and all documents. I compiled everything into a PDF.

109
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:43,999
I then sent that email. While sending it, I made just one sincere prayer — placing my hands on the laptop screen…

110
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:53,999
“Mother, You must reach there faster than this mail does.” After that, I closed my laptop.

111
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:59,999
But before I could even close it fully, the professor called me! I was completely shocked.

112
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:05,999
He said, “I haven’t even read your documents. Because I already received them earlier.”

113
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:09,999
I was confused — I had only created that CV two days ago. I hadn’t sent it to anyone else. I asked him where he got it.

114
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:15,999
He said, “A lady named Vandana came and gave it to me. You know Vandana, right?”

115
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:20,999
I told him I didn’t know any Vandana. He told me to check my contact list. I checked — she wasn’t there.

116
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:26,999
Both of us searched through our contact lists. No sign of anyone named Vandana. We never saw or heard of her again.

117
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:31,999
She handed over the CV and disappeared. We never found her after that.

118
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:42,999
When I told my grandma, she immediately said, “That was Mother Mary. Didn’t you say, ‘Mother, reach there faster than this mail’?”

119
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,999
I believed it. That had to be Mother.

120
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:53,999
Later, the professor invited me to visit. He said, “If you like the place, continue with me. If not, you’re free to leave.”

121
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:59,999
I went there, saw all the facilities, and I liked everything.

122
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:07,999
I asked him just one thing — “Sir, I must always be allowed to go to church and attend Mass. If you have any issue with that, I won’t stay.”

123
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:14,999
He said, “I have no problem at all. You can always go to church.” He was a Hindu.

124
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:21,999
But he said, “Even I go to church sometimes, every Sunday.” I was happy to hear that.

125
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:36,999
That’s all I needed. I didn’t think twice after that. Everything regarding my admission went smoothly. The professor himself took the initiative and arranged everything.

126
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:44,999
I’m set to join next month. I had only asked Mother for an ordinary university, but she gave me a medical college!

127
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:49,999
I have no medical background, yet she placed me in a medical college — in the neuroscience department.

128
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:55,999
The project we’re working on is funded by the central government, a medical project.

129
00:12:56,000 --> 00:13:03,999
Half of the project is based in India, and the rest is in collaboration with partners in Australia.

130
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:09,999
The professor said if I ever need to travel abroad, he’ll arrange everything. “You can do whatever you want here,” he said.

131
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:15,999
For all this, I’m deeply thankful to Mother and to Holy Trinity. We continued our evangelical mission too.

132
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:21,999
We gave out newsletters not just to Christians but also to Hindus, and even Muslims.

133
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:34,999
Before distributing the tracts, we would always pray that it would reach the hands of those who truly need it — the hurting, the hopeless.

134
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:45,999
We’d ask God to ensure that the right person receives it. Before handing it over, we’d ask each person, “Do you have any objection to receiving this?”

135
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:52,999
Some people take papers and just crumple and throw them away. To avoid that, we ask for their permission first.

136
00:13:53,000 --> 00:14:06,999
Only if they say yes, we give them the tract. We go in person and give it with sincerity.

137
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:10,999
Similarly, we also go to nearby slum areas.

138
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:15,999
We prepare food at home ourselves and distribute it among people living in the slums.

139
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:23,999
They felt great joy. They always said, whenever we need food, God will send you at the correct time.

140
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:30,999
Hearing that gave us great happiness. In the same way, we would buy old clothes, wash them well, fold them,

141
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:35,999
pack them nicely and take them to give to them. Likewise, we used to visit the sick,

142
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:42,999
pray for them, and anoint their heads with oil from Kreupasanam, praying for them.

143
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:49,999
That’s how my mother made a covenant. Within that we have two testimonies.

144
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:56,999
My mother took the covenant, and I took the covenant in 2019. At that time, when I took the covenant,

145
00:14:57,000 --> 00:15:02,999
I didn't have any special thoughts or hardships. I made the covenant to love God more,

146
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:08,999
to grow closer to Jesus' mother, and because my daughter was growing up and facing challenges at her age,

147
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:12,999
I had just one goal: to make her grow closer to Jesus.

148
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:19,999
In the beginning, she was very good in her studies, scoring well in first class,

149
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:24,999
so she started to think she could do many things by herself.

150
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:28,999
I used to tell her, “No dear, without Mother Mary and Jesus, we have nothing.” In my life,

151
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:33,999
I haven’t given her anything else. If I’ve given her one thing, it's this:

152
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:40,999
believe firmly in Mother Mary and Jesus and live by that. Just like she said, Jesus spoke.

153
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:47,999
Live by what Mother says. That was the atmosphere I hoped for. And I received that fruit

154
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:54,999
through making the covenant. That’s the biggest thing I received. And also, I was suffering for two years

155
00:15:55,000 --> 00:16:00,999
from gas and acidity issues. After praying with this covenant oil,

156
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:06,999
I was healed. Later, my daughter had a car accident, and even then,

157
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:14,999
there was Mother’s protection. At that time, I was repeating covenant verses,

158
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:21,999
praying. Then people were saying a case might happen. After praying, we were told:

159
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:29,999
“You need to go to that hospital nearby.” They said to go and see the doctor.

160
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:33,999
We said we’re going to the child’s doctor.

161
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:38,999
But it was all a lie. When we went there, the child was walking around in good health.

162
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:45,999
In that sleepy moment, Mother told me, “Get up. Take your husband and daughter and go there

163
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:50,999
this evening itself.” That one word – though they had said, “Don't go, they'll come here,”

164
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:54,999
I said, “No, Mother told us to go.” So we went there,

165
00:16:55,000 --> 00:17:00,999
saw them, and found the child was perfectly fine.

166
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:06,999
At that time, they were upset with us. Still, no problem. We spoke to them and asked,

167
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:11,999
“Shall we give any compensation?” We returned home. After two days,

168
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:16,999
we called again and asked, “Do you need any compensation?” After two days, they said,

169
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:23,999
“No, you don’t need to give anything.” So, through Mother’s intercession, we got relief from that situation.

170
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:27,999
Through Mother and Jesus, we have received many blessings, big and small. We prayed for others too.

171
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:32,999
And we thank Jesus and the Holy Trinity.

172
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:40,999
Psalms 56:10 to 13 – In God, whose word I praise,

173
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:47,999
in the Lord, whose word I praise, in God I trust; I will not be afraid.

174
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:55,999
What can man do to me? O God, I am bound by vows to You;

175
00:17:56,000 --> 00:18:02,999
I will present my thank offerings to You. For You have delivered me from death

176
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:10,999
and my feet from stumbling, that I may walk before God in the light of life.

177
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:21,999
This daughter Amala and this sister Jaya are sharing their powerful covenant experiences

178
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:30,999
at the feet of Our Lady of Kreupasanam. The testimony of this daughter Amala

179
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:38,999
is a model covenant testimony. From beginning to end, she asks every decision to Mother Mary.

180
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:47,999
Mother gives her messages and situations. She organizes her life

181
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:54,999
according to the messages given by Mother. She mentioned the struggles she faced during her master’s studies.

182
00:18:55,000 --> 00:19:01,999
From a young age, she has grown in deep spirituality and remained faithful in the covenant.

183
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:07,999
Even while standing in strong faith in the covenant,

184
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:16,999
her life was filled with suffering. People who did not understand her came into authority over her,

185
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:23,999
just like Pharaoh who didn’t understand Joseph in Egypt.

186
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:31,999
What came afterward was hardship for Joseph and slavery for the Israelites.

187
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:40,999
Likewise, in her life too, people who didn’t understand her value and quality –

188
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:46,999
those teachers who couldn’t recognize her goodness – instead of love, gave anger, instead of help, they created obstacles.

189
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:54,999
My daughter said the Dean gave her a really hard time, but my Heavenly Mother held her hand and led her forward.

190
00:19:55,000 --> 00:20:03,999
My daughter said, she made me a topper. While I was writing my dissertation, my thesis guide made things very difficult for me.

191
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:10,999
She didn’t give me any of the support I needed. And when someone else abandoned their dissertation,

192
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:18,999
I was forced to do that one too — just because I insisted I wouldn’t miss the Holy Mass.

193
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:27,999
I told them I wouldn’t compromise on that, that I would never skip daily Mass. When I told that to my guide,

194
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:33,999
a non-believer, she used it as a reason to mentally and emotionally harass me.

195
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:40,999
Still, my Heavenly Mother kept leading me step by step. My daughter says, even during exams,

196
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:49,999
I didn’t know what to write — I was about to close my pen and hand in a blank paper. I was sitting there, giving up.

197
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:55,999
Just as I stood up, someone came to me and said, “Sit back down. write what you know.”

198
00:20:56,000 --> 00:21:03,999
And then, answers just started flowing into my ears — continuously,

199
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:09,999
as if they were being poured directly into my mind. I wrote down each one and completed the paper.

200
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:15,999
When my course was over, I graduated with a gold medal. My Heavenly Mother helped me win that.

201
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:22,999
Even though I had done so much for my dissertation, they were still not satisfied.

202
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:29,999
I only had a few days left to finish it — the deadline was gone. I cried out again to Mother, saying:

203
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:37,999
“What do I do now? I’m losing everything I worked for.” Then my daughter says, Mother herself

204
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:44,999
showed me something on the internet and said, “Now, approach your topic in your own language,

205
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:51,999
in your own way.” In just a few hours — in three days — I rewrote almost an entire semester’s worth of work.

206
00:21:52,000 --> 00:22:00,999
I completed the dissertation and submitted it. The university considered it one of the best.

207
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:07,999
That dissertation was taken as the top work in the subject and I was awarded the gold medal — the highest mark in the department.

208
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:17,999
But each time, I kept saying, “This is not mine. It’s not by my merit. It’s only by God’s grace.”

209
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:24,999
In the very moments I thought of giving up, my Heavenly Mother stirred my heart, awakened my mind,

210
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:32,999
gave speed to my hands, and helped me finish everything. My daughter says:

211
00:22:33,000 --> 00:22:39,999
I then desired to do a PhD. Again, I asked my Heavenly Mother, “What subject should I take?”

212
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:45,999
The answer I got from Mother was “Neuroscience.” It didn’t have any strong link with microbiology, my earlier subject.

213
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:52,999
So everyone started asking, “How will you manage? Who will admit you? Which guide will consider you?” So many questions.

214
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:59,999
When questions came to my daughter, she had no answers because this was not her own decision — it was the communication of my Heavenly Mother.

215
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,999
This communication is deeply connected to the covenant. The covenant requires precise communication — whether we are exact and trustworthy.

216
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:15,999
Through the covenant, messages are clearly passed as words, as sentences, as individuals, as events — precisely like this, my Heavenly Mother

217
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:21,999
intervenes in our lives and keeps communicating in alignment with that divine appointment, my daughter says.

218
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:28,999
When she went back to the university and college, the Dean said how they could trouble her.

219
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:35,999
The HR also warned, “You don’t even have a single paper here in the university.”

220
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:41,999
But when she went there, with great joy, everything she needed was given to her, and those papers were released as her official documents.

221
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:48,999
Then she had obstacles to join for PhD because government funding was required.

222
00:23:49,000 --> 00:24:02,999
She realized the funding is currently stopped. She has to find a suitable professor and people who can help with this.

223
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:09,999
Not knowing how to find them, my daughter was anxious. Then Mother gave a message: “Pray with Daily Bread.”

224
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:14,999
She prayed with Daily Bread, added documents while her father blessed her,

225
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:21,999
and kept praying. Soon, she got a message that they found neuroscience researchers.

226
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:30,999
She read their profiles and got stuck on one. See how beautifully each one was selected.

227
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:38,999
She got stuck on one person, and then prepared two CVs. While preparing the CVs,

228
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:46,999
she told Mother one thing — before sending that email, Mother must go there first. That was the only instruction.

229
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:52,999
Before sending the email, Mother had to be there in person, to resolve any problems if they arose.

230
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:59,999
She is called “My Traveling Mother” — not just a name. Each of her children say that, coming from far away,

231
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:07,999
“My Traveling Mother walked ahead of me and arranged everything I needed.” My daughter sent the CV,

232
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:15,999
then turned off her laptop. Before long, her phone rang — who was it? That person called.

233
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:22,999
They said, “I already saw your matters beforehand. I am a professor who had no prior involvement or contact.

234
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:29,999
But your documents came to my hands. Vandana gave this to me.”

235
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:36,999
Until now, Vandana has not been found. Vandana had given everything and told her to go meet there.

236
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:45,999
She went and joined the PhD. That’s how my daughter started her PhD studies at the medical college.

237
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:52,999
Dear friends, the uniqueness of this testimony is this: in every sentence, she kept saying,

238
00:25:53,000 --> 00:26:00,999
“I have only lived with trust in my Heavenly Mother. I have never missed my Holy Mass once, never missed my daily bread or any other prayer.”

239
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:07,999
I believed in all of them and prayed with desire. That’s why I received clear messages, clear directions, the right people,

240
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:15,999
and even in times of suffering, my Heavenly Mother passed on the courage and messages to overcome them.

241
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:22,999
This is the covenant. Only through the covenant can we experience such great divine protection, my daughter says.

242
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:31,999
This family received such great blessings. Short-time blessings, blessings without any human connections,

243
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:37,999
sending angels to arrange and make things auspicious. When one might think all possibilities have ended,

244
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:45,999
it is by grace alone — without merit — that my daughter was prepared to achieve great success and high medals.

245
00:26:46,000 --> 00:27:02,999
For all these experiences, we thank the Heavenly Mother and the Holy Virgin. With folded hands, we dedicate this testimony.

246
00:27:03,000 --> 00:27:08,999
These are extraordinary divine experiences, and now they can be yours too.

247
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:16,999
If you have not subscribed to this YouTube channel yet, please subscribe now.

248
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:21,000
Share this video with your friends and become the Lord’s spectators. [Music]
